sn56.9:2.1 starts: “When you talk, bhikkhus, you should talk about:
sn56.9:2.2 starts: “Therefore, bhikkhus, an exertion should be made to understand:
mn63:3.2 starts: “Here, venerable sir, while I was alone in meditation,
mn63:5.13 starts: until I know whether the man who wounded me was tall
mn63:5.15 starts: until I know whether the man who wounded me was dark
mn63:5.17 starts: until I know whether the man who wounded me lives
mn63:5.19 starts: until I know whether the bow that wounded me
mn63:5.21 starts: until I know whether the bowstring that wounded me
# superseded: mn63:5.23 starts: until I know whether the shaft that wounded me was wild
mn63:5.25 starts: until I know with what kind of feathers the shaft
# superseded: mn63:5.27 starts: until I know with what kind of sinew the shaft
mn63:5.29 starts: until I know what kind of arrowhead it was
mn63:7.3 starts: And what have I left undeclared?
sn35.121:18.1 none
mn146:6.16 none
mn146:6.19 starts: “Impermanent, venerable sir.”—
